No Python LSP available, but the import check + functional test already confirm correctness. Here's a summary of everything implemented:

---

**`app/auth.py`** — `require_api_key` now checks `X-API-Key` against `VALID_API_KEYS`, raises HTTP 401 with `"Invalid or missing API key"` when absent or unknown, and returns the mapped username on success.

**`app/main.py`** — six changes:

| Endpoint | Changes |
|---|---|
| `GET /tasks` | Added optional `status`, `priority`, `assigned_to` filters + `page` (default 1) / `page_size` (default 20) pagination. Filters applied sequentially, then sliced. |
| `POST /tasks` | New. Requires `Depends(require_api_key)`. Validates `project_id` exists in `projects` (404 if not). Auto-generates ID as `max id + 1`. Returns the created task with 201. |
| `PUT /tasks/{task_id}` | New. Requires auth. Uses `model_copy(update=...)` with `exclude_unset=True` for partial updates. Returns 404 if not found. |
| `DELETE /tasks/{task_id}` | New. Requires auth. Pops from list, returns 204. Returns 404 if not found. |

All patterns match the existing code style (`for` loops over in-memory lists, `HTTPException` for error responses, `Depends` for auth).
